<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Shakespeare returns four weeks after starting propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning. His hand is steadier: he can write a page before the script tires, though long drafts still ache and the signature at the foot of a page is the hardest part. He has had no dizziness, wheeze, cold hands, nightmares, low mood, or tiredness beyond the cold three weeks ago, which cleared without antibiotics or decongestants. He drinks about 10 standard drinks a week, no more than three on any day, and two cups of coffee. The occupational therapist&apos;s first appointment has not yet happened. He uses a heavier pen he bought himself. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication</td><td>Propranolol extended-release 60 mg for four weeks; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Writing</td><td>A page before tiring; signatures still hardest</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>About 10 drinks a week; no day above three</td></tr><tr><td>Occupational therapy</td><td>Not yet seen; on the waiting list</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

